Found 2026-08-28 by the orchestrating agent while checking documentation.

  API_DOCKER_TEST_HOST=unix:///run/user/1000/podman/podman.sock prove -lr t/
  -> Files=38, Tests=423, Result: FAIL
     t/entity_container.t  (Wstat: 65280, exited 255) Tests: 2 Failed: 1
       not ok - undef isa 'API::Docker::Type::ContainerSummary'
       Can't call method "id" on an undefined value at t/entity_container.t line 52

CAUSE, and it is a one-line omission rather than anything deep.

test_docker() is a dual-mode helper: under API_DOCKER_TEST_HOST it returns a
REAL client and ignores the routes it was handed (t/lib/Test/API/Docker/Mock.pm
line 232). So any subtest built on fixture CONTENT has to opt out of live mode.
t/entity_container.t knows this and does it twice -- line 75 and line 109 both
carry `plan skip_all => 'fixture-only' if is_live();` -- and the subtest at
line 44 ("the generated classes are still the model, not a wrapper around it")
was missed. It asserts the fixture's abc123def456 and size_root_fs 187654321,
and this machine has no containers, so ->list returns [] and $c is undef.

The default fixture-only suite stays green, which is why nothing caught it.

SECOND, AND THE REASON THIS IS NOT MERELY A TEST FIX:

CLAUDE.md line 147 says "That run is green (26 files, 289 tests)." It is
38 files and 423 tests, and it is not green. A written-down measurement that
nobody re-measures is worse than no measurement -- it is what a reader trusts
instead of running the command. Either re-measure it as part of whatever
touches the live path, or replace the number with the command and let the
reader find out.

Note the same failure mode was already fixed once today in rule 11, which
claimed a fixed count of lib files.

